# C06 same request recover — factory stays closed

Issue: https://github.com/liboyang42-cpu/chengyin-remote-ops/issues/5
Repo: github.com/liboyang42-cpu/chengyin-ios
Branch: cursor/c06-same-request-recover-e504
Base: cursor/c06-manage-draft-read-e504 @ 27970a72891847d40d55b4dca461e3b34008a6ed

`MerchantNPCKnowledgeAuthorFlow.submitForOriginalReview` stores the one request
id it already received on that same flow, together with the member id already on
that author request. A ticket whose request id differs is not stored.
`readHeldThemeDraft` uses `heldThemeDraftMemberID` and `heldThemeDraftRequestID`
from that flow. It does not require the caller to pass an id submit did not
produce. A missing stored id returns before the reader, so it does not GET and
does not publish. `recoverFromDraftRead` returns nil and does not change phase
when the returned id differs.

The character page stays the existing character fields. The nested manage page
stays `MerchantStoreCharacterView` plus the manage `NavigationLink` into
`MerchantOperationsDocumentView`. This hunk does not replace either page.

## Not applied

The factory still builds the flow before submit, so `heldThemeDraftMemberID` and
`heldThemeDraftRequestID` are nil at construction. Copying those nils into the
manage link is not a page close. That attach is only the paste below. Do not
apply it. Do not edit:

```
App/AppSession.swift
App/AppCompositionRoot.swift
Questify.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj
```

Not inserted into `merchantOperationsDestination`. `publisher` stays nil. The
factory does not mint a second request id. It passes the same flow. Submit on
that flow is what stores the one request id. Do not read the construction-time
heldThemeDraftRequestID or heldThemeDraftMemberID as the read key.

```swift
if destination == .character,
   let merchantID = access.identity.merchantID,
   let row = PublicMerchantRowID(merchantID),
   let scope = merchantNPCScope(row: row) {
    let flow = MerchantNPCKnowledgeAuthorFlow(
        scope: scope,
        publisher: nil,
        currentScope: { [weak self] in self?.merchantNPCScope(row: row) })
    var caller: MerchantNPCThemeDraftRequestRead? = nil
    if let api = regionalConfiguration?.apiConfiguration {
        caller = MerchantNPCThemeDraftRequestRead(
            configuration: api,
            transport: runtimeHTTPTransport,
            memberID: { [weak self] in self?.account.map { Int64($0.id) } },
            token: { [weak self] in self?.token })
    }
    return merchantStoreCharacterDestination(
        authorFlow: flow,
        themeDraftRequestRead: caller)
}

NavigationLink {
    MerchantOperationsDocumentView(
        reader: npcSaveReader,
        destination: .character,
        authorFlow: authorFlow,
        themeDraftRequestRead: themeDraftRequestRead)
} label: { Text("manage", tableName: "MerchantNPCSaveReceipt") }
MerchantStoreCharacterView(coordinator: StoreCharacterCoordinator(reader: StoreCharacterOperationsReader(reader: reader)))
```

The paste passes `caller` into the existing nested manage destination. It does
not drop that value. It does not snapshot nil held ids. It does not mint. The
manage editor calls the read after submitForOriginalReview stores the id on the
same flow. Not inserted.

XCTest / App / CI = NOT_RUN where swiftc is absent. Not 100%.
